+# Contributing to AdaptixC2 v2.0
+
+## Project architecture
+
+AdaptixC2 v2.0 uses `adaptix.spec` as the project-level source of truth for repository layout, dependencies, package sets, runtime profile location, and systemd settings. `AdaptixTools` (`axtool`) provides the supported project/build interface.
+
+The main repository paths are:
+
+- `AdaptixServer/` — teamserver and extenders.
+- `AdaptixClient/` — Qt GUI client.
+- `AdaptixTools/` — project-aware build/install tooling.
+- `adaptix.spec` — v2.0 project definition.
+- `dist/` — generated runtime/release staging tree; do not commit it.
+
+Do not introduce a second build model in CI when the same operation is already represented by `axtool` or the project Makefile.
+
+## Local checks
+
+From the repository root, use Go 1.26.5 or a compatible 1.26.x toolchain:
+
+```bash
+cd AdaptixTools
+go test ./...
+go vet ./...
+go build -buildvcs=false -o dist/axtool .
+cd ..
+make tools
+./dist/axtool validate ./AdaptixServer/extenders/beacon_listener_http
+```
+
+For the server/package integration path on Linux:
+
+```bash
+./dist/axtool adaptix.spec server build --gen-cert -d
+./ci/integration.sh ./dist/adaptixserver ./dist/profile.yaml
+```
+
+The integration script starts the generated server, checks the TLS listener and runtime HTTPS response, verifies the runtime layout, and always cleans up the process.
+
+## axtool architecture rules
+
+Prefer changing `AdaptixTools` when build/install semantics need to change. Avoid duplicating those semantics in shell scripts or GitHub Actions.
+
+The important v2.0 flow is:
+
+```text
+adaptix.spec
+  -> project/spec resolution
+  -> build
+  -> install/state/workspace/profile
+  -> dist/
+  -> integration tests
+  -> release artifacts
+```
+
+Extender packages are described by `axtool.spec`. Their build and release metadata should remain the source of truth for package installation.
+
+## CI and release
+
+Pull requests should exercise formatting, tests, vetting, `axtool` validation, and Linux server/package integration. Security analysis is separate from the normal build path. Releases are tag-driven and must not publish untested artifacts.
+
+When adding a new generated artifact, make sure it is either intentionally uploaded by CI or ignored locally. Do not commit credentials, runtime certificates, or `axtool` installation state.
